module main

from lib import measure

# plans/M9.md item A1b, decision 15 / item JJ decision 182: `eval::interp`
# walks one `TypedProgram`'s flat name tables and has no notion of which
# module a body came from, so an imported body is evaluated against *this*
# module's tables. `measure`'s body reaches `Priv`, which only `lib` has —
# a declaration present only in a private helper, not in any imported
# signature. That is a real boundary, and it says so by name (no longer
# citing closed item A1b for the wording). Before A1b the same program
# abandoned with `internal error: struct `Priv` not found`, which is a
# bug by house rule (CLAUDE.md), not an outcome.
pub const N: u32 = measure()
